  "controller_actions": [
    {
      "op": "spawn",
      "role": "builder",
      "task": "Write module.py and test_cases.json. module.py: solve(data) per the user contract. Process data['ops'] in order without mutating input; keep balance and a dict of active holds (id->amount); held = sum of holds; available = balance - held. Per-op check order: (1) kind in credit/debit/hold/release else ValueError; (2) for credit/debit/hold, amount must be int (not bool) and >=1 else ValueError; (3) hold: id must not be an active hold; release: id must be an active hold, else ValueError (release ignores amount); (4) debit/hold: amount must not exceed available else ValueError. credit adds to balance, debit subtracts, hold adds a hold, release removes it. Return {'balance','held','available'}; an empty list returns zeros. Standard library only, no I/O. test_cases.json: JSON list of at least 8 distinct cases, each with 'input' and exactly one of 'output' or 'error' (exception class name, e.g. ValueError). Cover: empty ops, credit+debit, hold and release, release ignoring amount, bool amount error, amount 0 error, unknown kind error, duplicate hold id error, release of unknown id error, debit exceeding available funds (due to hold) error, hold exceeding available error, and check-order cases (e.g. unknown kind with bad amount, invalid amount on a hold with duplicate id). Expectations must match the contract."
    },
    {
      "op": "wait"
    },
    {
      "op": "run_tests"
    },
